<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n87926" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόλημμα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, τό</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>something taken beforehand,
				advantage,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ποιεῖν τινι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					18.10.3
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>BGU</u>
				775.12
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii A.D.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>prepossession, prejudice,</i> compared to a <i>previous
				disease</i> of the soul, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Corp.Herm.</u>
				12.3
			</span></i> (pl.).</div>
